								<div id="contentForThisGame_ctn">
				</div>
									<div data-panel="{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;PanelGroup&quot;}" id="aboutThisGame" class="game_page_autocollapse" style="max-height: 850px;">
						<div id="game_area_description" class="game_area_description">
							<h2>About This Game</h2>
							<p class="bb_paragraph" >Mogged: Looksmaxx or Die is a 1–8 player <strong>proximity voice chat</strong> co-op horror comedy game about getting hot before something at the party gets you. Featuring fun physics and a tight extraction loop.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4917440/extras/2a4a95996f03dd6f2638d55ce5e9b932.poster.avif?t=1791114490" width=1170 height=670 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4917440/extras/2a4a95996f03dd6f2638d55ce5e9b932.webm?t=1791114490" type="video/webm; codecs=vp9"><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4917440/extras/2a4a95996f03dd6f2638d55ce5e9b932.mp4?t=1791114490" type="video/mp4"></video></span></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >You and your friends made a pact to improve your looks each week, in an ever-rising quota. Fail to improve, and you surrender to hopelessness together. Game over.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >THE LOOP</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>LOOKSMAXX BY DAY</strong><br>Buy supplies, softmaxx, and get presentable. Even the door guy won't let you into the party if you're too chopped.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>PARTY BY NIGHT</strong></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Rummage through frat-house cabinets for looksmaxxing contraband while something inside stalks the ugliest person it can find. Keep the operation discreet and, more importantly, stay prettier than at least one of your friends.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>BE HOME BY 5AM</strong></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Anything still on you after curfew gets confiscated. Sell your extra gear to fund your ascension.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Repeat.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >If you've done well, congratulations: the quota goes up.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" > <br>If your group comes up short, don't panic. Diversify into illegal pharmaceuticals, sketchy procedures, stock trading, or gainful employment. Whatever gets the average higher.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4917440/extras/491466c1ffc6d65a40e2b58e508639c0.poster.avif?t=1791114490" width=1170 height=670 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4917440/extras/491466c1ffc6d65a40e2b58e508639c0.webm?t=1791114490" type="video/webm; codecs=vp9"><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4917440/extras/491466c1ffc6d65a40e2b58e508639c0.mp4?t=1791114490" type="video/mp4"></video></span></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >THE PROGRESSION</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >Being prettier than your friends keeps you alive. Being prettier than the quota keeps the run alive.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Start as a sub3 and drag your looks toward 10 through stolen products, questionable procedures, and increasingly experimental research peptides. Stack enough compounds and you might even push past the genetic hand you were dealt.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Fill your dorm with equipment designed to protect your aura, manage your cortisol. </p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Build your underground pharma business. Get rehired at your job, and even LARP with a Ferrari if you need.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >And when looksmaxxing stops being enough, there are always more aggressive forms of mogging.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >THE ENVIRONMENT</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >APARTMENT<br>Your safe space.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >MAXMART<br>Everything you need to softmaxx the responsible way. Skincare, groceries, bananas.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >THE YARD<br>A forest road connecting civilization to the frat house. Scenic by day. A terrible place to be ugly after dark.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >FRAT HOUSE (Procedurally Generated)</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Your primary source of looksmaxxing contraband. Blend into the party, mog the guests, and steal anything that might raise the group average. Whatever is inside has standards. Track your steps and get home BEFORE 5AM.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >BASEMENT LAB</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Your pharmaceutical headquarters. Mix groceries with research chemicals, test experimental doses on your friends, write the effects on the label, and sell the batch to somebody with even worse judgment. Occasionally, grind a friend into a high quality ingredient. Keep a fire extinguisher nearby.  </p><p class="bb_paragraph" > <br>KEY FEATURES</p><ul class="bb_ul"><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >Deep Looksmaxxing progression </p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >Randomly generated frat party extraction levels</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >An ever-rising looks quota to meet</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >Looks are gameplay</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >The ugliest player gets hunted</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >15 enemies</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >1–8 Player Proximity Voice Chat Co-op</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" >Shotguns</p></li></ul><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p>						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="game_page_autocollapse">
		<div id="game_area_content_descriptors" class="game_area_description">
			<h2>AI Generated Content Disclosure</h2>
			<p>The developers describe how their game uses AI Generated Content like this:</p>
			<p><i>
					AI tools were used in a limited way to help generate parts of some in-game comedic images and voice barks, which were then edited, refined, and finalized by human artists.				</i>
			</p>
					</div>
	</div>
		<div class="game_page_autocollapse">
		<div id="game_area_content_descriptors" class="game_area_description">
			<h2>Mature Content Description</h2>
			<p>The developers describe the content like this:</p>
			<p><i>
			MOGGED is a horror comedy about looksmaxxing culture. It contains:<br />
<br />
Violence and gore. Players and NPCs are killed with fists, a hammer and a shotgun. There is blood, corpses and ragdolls. One machine in the game grinds bodies into meat.<br />
<br />
Drugs and alcohol. The game is built around performance enhancing drugs. Players inject peptides and steroids, some named after real substances, and can manufacture and sell them. Beer and cigarettes can be consumed. Characters speak favourably about drug use. The tone is satirical and the drugs carry side effects, but the subject is central to the game.<br />
<br />
Self-harm. The game references bonesmashing, a real practice where people strike their own face to change its bone structure. It is not something to try. In the game, using the hammer for bonesmashing provides an insignificant, nearly immeasurable improvement at the cost of significantly injuring your player.<br />
<br />
Horror. Sudden scares, stalking enemies and dark environments.<br />
<br />
Language and humor. Swearing and crude jokes about bodies, death, mental health and drug use.<br />
<br />
Online. The game has open voice chat. Valve does not rate what other players say.				</i>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	
				
				
